{
  "surface": "notifications",
  "route": "/notifications",
  "notes": "The notification centre's Alerts feed (#1391) at the address the bell opens, with two of the fixture account's rows: one unread with the type's icon and dot, one read. `origin` is the list, so the measurement is the page's row anatomy and the gaps inside it, not where the site's tabs end and the app begins; `capture` is the list, the region both clients draw identically. The empty state is the page's own frame when the account has no notifications. The relative time is the fixture's (`two hours`, `three days`), so the clock is not in the recording, and the words come from the surface's generated copy (ADR-0104).",
  "motion": {
    "notes": "The settled feed is still; a row fades its background and its icon surface on hover with the same colour transition, and the page's loading face is a pulse skeleton. The app draws no travel on a row, so the same means the same colour change.",
    "entries": []
  },
  "states": [
    {
      "name": "at-rest",
      "route": "/notifications?tab=alerts",
      "origin": "notifications-list",
      "capture": "notifications-list",
      "elements": [
        {
          "name": "notifications-list",
          "web": {
            "selector": "[data-visual='notifications-list']"
          },
